# YubiKey PIV authentication (slot 9A).
#
# Identities come from ssh-agent, which has the PKCS#11 module loaded
# (see ~/.config/systemd/user/ssh-agent.service and `yk-reload`).
#
# Deliberately NO PKCS11Provider line here. Loading the module in both the
# agent and ssh opens two competing PIV sessions on the token; the direct load
# evicts the agent's cached PIN and signing then fails with
# "agent refused operation".
#
# IdentityFile + IdentitiesOnly are kept on purpose: the token exposes six keys
# over PKCS#11 (slot 9A, four age-plugin-yubikey retired slots, attestation)
# and the agent offers all of them. Servers with the default MaxAuthTries of 6
# reject the connection before reaching the right one. IdentitiesOnly restricts
# what is offered to the identities listed here -- it applies to agent-provided
# keys too, not just files, so it still works without PKCS11Provider.

Host *
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_yubikey_piv.pub
    IdentitiesOnly yes

Host github.com
    User git

Host gitlab.com
    User git
